body:
**Validation run result (2026-11-21, CamCraft 0.24.0):** our Sodick output for the owner's 10 mm square, compared with his known-good `demoprog.txt`. The Sodick post today writes 1-pass, untapered programs only. To match the owner's program it still needs:

- the condition block written in the program (`C000 = ...`, `C001 = ...`) - needs the control fields (ON, OFF, IP, SV ...) stored per condition; the machine file holds only gap, wire diameter and role (#3183);
- the H table (`H000`, `H001`) with `G42`/`G40` control-side offset (today the offset is baked into the path, so the operator cannot trim size at the control);
- `TP`/`TN`, and the start sequence in the owner's order: `G90`, `T94`, `G29`, `T84`, `G54`, `G00 X Y`, `Z0`, `U0 V0` reset, `T91`, `FLAG7 D` (we write `T84`/`T94` after `T91`, and no `G29`, `Z0`, `U0 V0`, `FLAG7`);
- `M03` thread-jump point; end block `G349 G449 G549 G649 G749`, `G149 G249`, `T87`, `M35`;
- skims (refused today: "a condition change between passes (skims) is not supported by this post") and taper/4-axis (refused: "the Sodick wire post writes a vertical 2-axis cut only");
- the program number and comment from `set_program` (not written today).

Already right: decimal point on every number, no feed word, `T90` / `M02`. To confirm with the owner: his `G42` with counter-clockwise travel puts the wire outside the 10 mm square (punch side); our cut was die side.

Related issues from the same run: #3206 (P1 wire-iso decimals), #3207, #3209, #3213, #3214, #3215.
